    "body": "STOPPED at Step 5. Claim released. No fix or PR was pushed.\n\nI added the Windows pin first on the head of PR #3026. I started this command on the unchanged helper:\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm the_windows_x86_64_bore_count_pin_is_exact -- --exact --nocapture`\n\nThis host has only the x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu target. It has no Windows runtime or cross compiler. `rustc --print cfg` confirms target_os=\"linux\". The Windows pin is excluded on this host. I stopped the build because it cannot execute that pin. I did not obtain the required failing test. The build output is local at /tmp/3050-pin-red.txt.\n\nThe Windows branch of bore_path_matches still pins (4716, 4688, 549). This report does not claim that the Windows bug is fixed.\n\nPRs #3026, #3027, and #3010 change bore_path_matches and the same bore test. I based the temporary branch on #3026, as the overlap rule requires. I removed the temporary test without changing the helper. I did not run mutations or gates.\n\nThe next attempt needs a Windows x86_64 host to prove the failure and run the requested heavy gate.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
