    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T19:56:49Z",
    "body": "Linux reading, for the pin of this platform:\n\n- Host: Linux x86_64 (`x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`).\n- Commit: unchanged `upstream/main` at 3c761b5bb.\n- Command: `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm -- --ignored --exact the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`\n- Result: the test fails at `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs:144`. The counts are (3158, 3130, 1141). The Linux x86_64 pin is (4726, 4698, 549).\n\nThe Linux counts are equal to the macOS aarch64 pin and to the new Windows counts in this issue. Thus the three platforms now give the same triple.\n\nI found this in the heavy run of PR #3055. That PR changes only the assets lookup of `crates/post/src/data_dir.rs`, and the same failure occurs on main without it.\n",
